<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Sesame agent entitlements — MINIMAL by design (pinned decision #4).

	  Hardened Runtime is applied via `codesign -o runtime` (a signing flag, not
	  an entitlement) — required for notarization and to run SE crypto under a
	  trusted runtime.

	  NOT sandboxed: the agent writes the ciphertext vault under Application
	  Support and opens a Unix-domain socket in the login session — both of which
	  the App Sandbox would block. So the sandbox entitlement is explicitly false.

	  NO keychain-access-groups: the Secure-Enclave key is a keychain token item
	  under the app's OWN default access group (decision #3); a signed app reaches
	  its own items with no special entitlement — that key is only for CROSS-app
	  keychain sharing (and is a paid/restricted entitlement). Adding it would be
	  wrong here. If a future SE operation is rejected for a missing entitlement,
	  document the exact key and add ONLY that one.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<false/>
</dict>
</plist>
